  "lead_raw_text": " The structure of MnAg₂ (Mn₂Ag₄ per cell) crystallizes in the trigonal space group P-31m (No. 143), with six atoms in the unit cell distributed over three independent Wyckoff orbits. Geometry-derived analysis shows both Ag and Mn centers in close-packed-like 12-neighbor environments: two orbits of four Ag atoms (Ag–Ag and Ag–Mn neighbors, 2.82–2.97 Å) and one Mn orbit of two Mn atoms (Mn–Ag neighbors, 2.82–2.89 Å). The geometric neighbor graph forms a single three-dimensional component spanning all six sites, and validated polyhedron contacts reveal corner-, edge-, and face-sharing among the 12-vertex Ag and Mn coordination polyhedra.\n<CRYSTAL_START>",
